@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: WHAT THIS REPORT RUNS</b>
  Group Consolidated Exposure | Party ACMCOR | report type risk
  --
  <b>THE WIZARD: THREE STEPS</b>
  --
  {#
    Step | What the step carries
    1 | the definition and the configurations it binds
    2 | the analytics, as the switchboard
    3 | review and save
  }
  [ Back ] | [ Next: the analytics ]
  --
  <b>STEP 1 - THE DEFINITION AND THE CONFIGURATIONS IT BINDS</b>
  --
  {#
    Configuration type | What it supplies | Where that data lives
    conventions | calendars, day counts, pairs | /refdata/conventions -> Conventions
    pricing_engines | engine per product family | NO SCREEN, no route exists
    todays_market | curves, surfaces, FX spots | NO SCREEN, no route exists
    curve_configuration | builder and pillars per curve | NO SCREEN, no route exists
    risk_report_config | the analytics and their settings | NO SCREEN, no route exists
  }
  Only conventions has a screen today: PATHS.conventions, /refdata/conventions.
  The other four are stated as missing, never drawn as links that would not resolve.
  Group risk configuration carries the analytics, and four definitions bind it:
  this one, Board Risk Dashboard, Group DV01 by book, Treasury Sensitivity.
  Everything steps 2 and 3 change reaches all four.
  --
  <b>STEP 2 - THE SWITCHBOARD: EVERY ANALYTIC TYPE, ONE ROW EACH</b>
  --
  {#
    Analytic | On | Order | Parameters
    npv | Y | 1 | discount_curve, include_cashflows
    sensitivity | Y | 2 | shift_size = 0.0001, shift_type = Absolute
    cashflow | N | 3 | bucket, include_fixings
    curves | no row | - | curve_set, build_on_the_fly
    portfolioDetails | Y | 4 | grouping, include_empty_books
    simulation | N | 5 | number_of_paths, seed, time_grid
    pfe | Y | 6 | horizon = 10, quantile = 0.95, exposure_cube
    saccr | N | 7 | reporting_currency, include_collateral
    parametricVar | no row | - | confidence, horizon_days
    creditcurves | no row | - | hazard_rate_source, recovery_rate
    calibration | N | 8 | model, max_iterations, tolerance
    pnlExplain | no row | - | decomposition, threshold
    historicalSimulationVar | no row | - | confidence, lookback_days
    xva | no row | - | base_currency, methodology, include_cva
  }
  The parameters are summarised here. The controls live in the add-analytic flow.
  A type with no row has no switch: adding it is the flow, which writes the row.
  A row that is off stays on the configuration and reads as off. An analytic is
  turned off by setting active to false, never by deleting the row, so the
  history shows the report used to produce it.
  No control on this panel removes a row.
  {
    [ Add analytic ] - opens the add-analytic flow
  }
  --
  <b>THE RULE BETWEEN ANALYTICS, SHOWN AS A STATE</b>
  --
  <b>THIS SET CANNOT RUN: pfe is on and simulation is off.</b> Both rows above are marked.
  {
    [ simulation ] <color:red>OFF, staged - pfe is on, turning this off breaks it</color>
    [ pfe ] <color:red>ON, staged - needs simulation, cannot run</color>
  }
  pfe reads a cube that simulation writes. The rule lives in the ACME seeder, in
  generate_risk_config_data.py, check_exposure_needs_simulation, and in no service:
  the write would be accepted and the run would fail later.
  The screen refuses it itself and says that is what it is doing.
  --
  <b>THE ADD-ANALYTIC FLOW - SCREEN 1: THE LIST</b>
  --
  {#
    Analytic | What it produces | State
    npv | one present value per trade | on
    sensitivity | the change per market factor | on
    cashflow | cashflow rows, bucketed | off
    curves | the built curves and pillars | no row
    simulation | simulated paths and the cube | off, staged
    saccr | standardised credit exposure | off
    parametricVar | one value at risk figure | no row
    portfolioDetails | trades and notional per book | on
    creditcurves | survival probability per name | no row
    pfe | exposure profile and one figure | on, staged
    calibration | fitted parameters and fit error | off
    pnlExplain | yesterday's P&L split by factor | no row
    historicalSimulationVar | a value at risk from history | no row
    xva | CVA, DVA and funding cost | no row
  }
  [ Choose ] and nothing is written.
  --
  <b>THE ADD-ANALYTIC FLOW - SCREEN 2: THE DETAIL, READ THREE WAYS</b>
  --
  <b>A document</b>   a short readable page, then every parameter in one column
  <b>B two columns</b> explanation and calculation left, settings and effect right
  <b>C guided</b>      one parameter at a time, the explanation beside it, a summary last
  {#
    The analytic | pfe is how large the book could become against a counterparty
    How calculated | reads the cube simulation writes, takes a quantile by date
  }
  {#
    Parameter | Control | Meaning and a normal value
    horizon | number field | days forward; normal 10
    quantile | number field | confidence read at; normal 0.95
    exposure_cube | text field, DEFERRED | the cube it reads; the cube simulation wrote
  }
  The control follows the parameter's shape: number field for a count, select for
  an enumeration, toggle for a boolean, text field for a name.
  <b>DEFERRED:</b> simulation and pfe need purpose-built editors for the cube, the
  shift and the time grid. They are drawn as plain fields here, and the page says
  so on the parameter. A plain field is not the design.
  --
  <b>THE ADD-ANALYTIC FLOW - SCREEN 3: THE EFFECT</b>
  --
  The next run of every definition bound to Group risk configuration produces it.
  It writes one analytic row and one parameter row per parameter.
  A run after the change is not comparable with one before it.
  <b><color:red>REFUSED: pfe needs simulation, and it is off in the set on the table.</color></b>
  {
    [ Turn simulation on as well ] | [ Back to the settings ] | [ Cancel ]
  }
  --
  <b>STEP 3 - REVIEW AND SAVE: EXACTLY WHAT WILL BE WRITTEN</b>
  --
  {#
    Field | Was | Will be
    simulation.active | Y | N, row kept at display_order 5
    pfe.active | N | Y, display_order 6
    pfe.exposure_cube | simulation-cube-01 | unchanged
  }
  <b>NOT WRITABLE YET: this set cannot run.</b> Step 2 has to turn simulation on,
  or turn pfe off, before the wizard offers the write.
  No row is deleted and no run is started.
  --
  <b>WHAT THE CHANGE DOES AND DOES NOT REACH</b>
  --
  Past runs keep the configuration they ran with, with their outputs and errors.
  The configuration is shared, so every definition bound to it runs the new set on
  its next run, including the three the person did not open.
  A run after the change is not comparable with a run before it: the two runs did
  not produce the same measures. The results screen marks a comparison partial
  where a side carried errors, and cannot mark this case, because nothing says
  which configuration version a run used.
  --
  <b>RUNS THE CHANGE MAKES INCOMPARABLE</b>
  --
  {#
    Run | Started | Configuration it ran with
    run 41c9f0a7 | 2026-10-16 06:04 | inference from start time
    run 5b02e6d3 | 2026-10-15 06:03 | inference from start time
  }
  --
  <b>WHAT THIS SCREEN CANNOT SHOW</b>
  --
  A screen for four of the five configuration types: none exists, only conventions
  has a route. The purpose-built editors for the cube, the shift and the time grid:
  deferred. Which configuration version a run used: not readable. A configuration's
  own version history: not readable. Whether pfe without simulation is refused: it
  is not, by any service.
  The screen states these absences rather than drawing a validation it does not have.
}

@enduml
